Dawn chants wake garland-slipped Rāvaṇa brooding on Sītā --- Lust-driven Rāvaṇa enters jeweled Aśōkavana with ponds and beasts --- Hundred wives follow bearing lamps fans water swords liquor and parasol --- Hanumān hears anklets and sees lamp-lit Rāvaṇa like bowless Kāma --- Hanumān hides in leaves recognizing Viśravas son nearing Sītā
